{
  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "The current best (config_018, acc=0.619) uses multimodal + multiprofile + pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat. The most under-explored high-impact axis is the image encoder: we have only tested ResNet50, while ViT-L (imagenet_vit_l) is a substantially more powerful backbone. Since adding image already improved accuracy by ~4 pts over RNA-only (0.527 vs 0.485), a stronger image encoder could yield a meaningful gain in the already-strong multiprofile/avgpool/concat setting. Config_024 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) from the current best, isolating that effect. This is preferred over testing fusion (config_019, where concat≈weighted is already near-confirmed) or RNA encoder swaps, because the image encoder represents the largest untested capacity lever. With 4 experiments left, a strong result here would anchor the remaining budget around ViT-L-based configurations, while a null result would confirm ResNet50 suffices and redirect effort to RNA encoder or other axes."
}

